  <text>
    <body>
      <conceptEntry id="dpp-0132">
      <languageSection xml:lang="eng">
          <descrip type="definition">
            <p>digital twin reconstructed from point-in-time attestations about the object, sampled when the object visits an attestor, in which truth is episodic and staleness between attestations is unbounded and undetectable</p>
          </descrip>
          <note type="note">Corresponds to capability classes S0 (silent, testimony-only) and S1 (passive authentication).</note>
          <note type="note">Trust rides entirely on attestor authority; the twin is testimonial by default and sensorial by exception.</note>
          <ref>UniDPP PLAN (2026-09) Passive twin → active twin: the paradigm axis</ref>
      </languageSection>
      </conceptEntry>
    </body>
  </text>
</tbx>
